+# P0 continuation primitives: engineering interface
+
+This code is a candidate building block, not an experiment protocol, actual
+preflight receipt, or launch clearance. No data, step count, split, optimizer
+configuration, device budget, or model is selected by this module. The
+independent protocol reviewer must approve those separately.
+
+An arm manifest (`SI_CONTINUATION_DATA_V1`) binds `arm` B or C, the base and
+P0 adapter tree hashes, the exact `training_config`, and a JSONL dataset hash.
+Its `sample_schedule` lists every dataset sample exactly once with its explicit
+`sample_id`, `task_group`, and integer `exposures`; the dataset provides those
+same identifiers plus `prompt` and `completion`. The `ordered_sample_ids`
+array gives the full order, including repetitions across distinct passes; it
+must exactly match the per-sample exposure counts. There is no reshuffle.
+Epoch lengths and whether each sample must appear exactly once per epoch are
+explicit, and declared task-group exposure totals must match the full order.
+The dataset review JSON is itself hashed and binds the dataset hash, arm, and
+SHA-256 of those schedule, order, epoch and task-exposure fields encoded as
+compact UTF-8 JSON with sorted keys. Its
+`PASS_DATA_ONLY` field is a binding interface, not an authentication of the
+reviewer or an independent scientific verdict. A separate gate must validate
+the reviewer and full experiment protocol. The `compare_initial_conditions`
+helper checks identical B/C model, P0 and training config; it does not certify
+task isolation, matching, token balance, or independence.
+
+The adapter is loaded with PEFT's `is_trainable=True` from the supplied P0,
+then the saved adapter tensors are compared to the loaded tensors and only
+LoRA parameters may be trainable. Both arms must be separately initialized.
+The module performs no evaluation or best-checkpoint selection and saves only
+the final adapter after successful completion. A fresh output path is required.
+The journal records start/completion of model loading, microbatches and
+optimizer steps, including sample IDs and task groups. Started forward tokens
+are conservatively charged even when a forward fails; completion is separate.
+The input ceiling counts non-padding full input IDs including completion. Both
+padded and non-padding inputs and causally supervised tokens are recorded. The mean
+loss of each microbatch is weighted by its active causal label tokens over the
+whole optimizer update. AdamW fused or non-fused mode, gradient checkpointing,
+and the warmup/cosine schedule are explicit frozen settings. The recorded LR
+is the LR actually applied at each optimizer step. No mode falls back silently.
+For update `s` from 1 through `N`, warmup `W`, base rate `L` and floor ratio
+`r`, the rate is `L*s/W` when `s <= W`, otherwise
+`L*(r+(1-r)/2*(1+cos(pi*(s-W)/(N-W))))`. This exact convention is an explicit
+candidate protocol choice and is not claimed to match historical HF Trainer.
+EOS is explicitly supervised and overlength rows are rejected, not truncated.
+
+The wall clock check is cooperative: it cannot interrupt a blocked model load,
+forward, save, device cleanup, initial hash calculation, or process shutdown.
+A separate single-use CLI supervisor is provided as candidate code; its
+independent exact-SHA review, production preflight and release are still
+required. It must enforce hard wall/device-time, resource and cleanup bounds
+and record an authentic exit before any live launch can be accepted.
+Injected loaders enable CPU tests; production launch must bind the local-only
+loaders and exact environment/source independently. Hashing follows individual
+file links in the HF cache and hashes resolved bytes; directory links fail.
+The reviewed data files and frozen inputs are rechecked before final save.
+Partially written outputs and begun operations must be retained on failure;
+there is no automatic retry. None of this authorizes a GPU/model invocation.
+
+The interpreter bytes and full Python version, plus the versions, actual
+entrypoints and entire package source/resource/binary trees of torch, peft,
+transformers, tokenizers, safetensors, accelerate and huggingface_hub, are
+bound by the independently reviewed runtime identity. Package trees use
+Python `Path` component lexicographic ordering over relative paths; the SHA256
+input is compact UTF-8 JSON of `[relative_path, size, file_sha256]` records.
+Only `__pycache__` directories and `.pyc`/`.pyo` files are omitted; symlinks
+are rejected. Static preflight reads file origins and distribution metadata
+without importing these packages. An authenticated worker imports each and
+writes a separate actual-origin/version/hash receipt before model work. This
+does not fingerprint external shared libraries or the entire environment.
+
+The static CLI preflight binds both arm manifests, common P0/model/optimizer,
+protocol bytes, a separately reviewed pair decision, arm review, interpreter,
+exact environment, budget, output path and unique run ID. It must not load a
+tokenizer or model, initialize CUDA, or construct an environment. A separate
+one-shot clearance binds its exact receipt. Software integration tests use only
+tiny locally generated CPU fixtures and cannot establish real-device behavior.
+The shared CUDA guard checks the UUID and signed allocator/global-free limits
+but makes no exclusive-device or device-wide ownership attribution claim.
+
+`run_si_continuation_engineering.py` is a separate engineering-only gate,
+preflight, clearance, worker and supervisor: its authorization has no dataset,
+task, evaluation or source-trajectory field. In its real-device mode the
+independently bound engineering plan permits only 32 synthetic sequences of
+length 2,048, two fused/checkpointed AdamW updates, and 1,200 seconds including
+cleanup. The model and existing P0 must match separately reviewed hashes. A
+unique engineering trial adapter is saved once, hashed and deleted; it is not
+eligible as a scientific checkpoint. The receipt records exact tokens,
+updates, losses, finite gradients, GPU allocator peaks, OOM/retry counters,
+artifact hash/deletion, real child exit and cleanup. Failure preserves events
+and forbids retry. Synthetic CPU tests are explicitly labelled software-only.
+
+The engineering projection includes all observed non-step supervisor time plus
+78 times the slower measured update, multiplied by 1.5; it must fit the frozen
+scientific-arm allocation. This is an engineering feasibility estimate, not a
+guarantee of shared-GPU availability, later training completion or model
+quality. Independent exact-SHA review and an engineering-only authorization and
+clearance are required before any real model or GPU invocation.
